WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.238
One government-cloud fact
shapes the exposure gate.

2
00:00:03.238 --> 00:00:08.066
Learn says Microsoft Security Exposure
Management, with its attack paths,

3
00:00:08.066 --> 00:00:11.103
exposure graph and
critical asset management,

4
00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:15.075
is available in Public Cloud
only, not in US Government clouds.

5
00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:18.957
Defender Vulnerability
Management is available in GCC,

6
00:00:18.957 --> 00:00:21.600
core and premium, without two features.

7
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.650
DeviceInfo still carries exposure level,
internet facing, and asset value.

8
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.413
And the vulnerability tables stay in
Defender; they aren't ingested into Sentinel.

9
00:00:31.413 --> 00:00:36.180
So the guide's interim path prioritizes
by those columns and Vulnerability

10
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.450
Management's recommendations, with the Tier
0 inventory as the critical-asset list.
